# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A lar root's three terms name one address"

# The root carries exactly three dot-separated terms — heading, angle of approach, carried dynamic
# — and each may stand as a word or a hyphen-joined compound. They name ONE address between them,
# so they share a family and a reader meets them as one thing.
#
# Painted from three families they read as three unrelated things: measured over the 65 bundled
# themes, all three shared a colour in 1 of them, and Gruvbox Dark Medium gave the heading aqua
# and the other two yellow. Under one family they read alike in all 65.
#
# The tails stay distinct, so a rule written against one term still reaches that term alone. No
# bundled theme rules below `entity.name.tag` for a scope this grammar emits, so the difference
# stands available rather than visible.

! Three plain terms

A lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/x here.
#        ^^ entity.name.tag.heading.lar.memetic-wikitext
#           ^^ entity.name.tag.angle.lar.memetic-wikitext
#              ^^ entity.name.tag.dynamic.lar.memetic-wikitext

! A hyphen-joined compound in the heading slot

A lar:///the-grid.walks.green/path here.
#        ^^^^^^^^ entity.name.tag.heading.lar.memetic-wikitext
#                 ^^^^^ entity.name.tag.angle.lar.memetic-wikitext
#                       ^^^^^ entity.name.tag.dynamic.lar.memetic-wikitext

! A hyphen-joined compound in every slot

A lar:///breach.watch-close.fires-now here.
#        ^^^^^^ entity.name.tag.heading.lar.memetic-wikitext
#               ^^^^^^^^^^^ entity.name.tag.angle.lar.memetic-wikitext
#                           ^^^^^^^^^ entity.name.tag.dynamic.lar.memetic-wikitext
